ov5693: Surface Pro 7 front camera fixes (binned mode, mirror option)

With the stock driver the 2x2-binned 1296x972 mode gives only "csi2-2 error:
Frame sync error" and empty buffers as soon as either flip is on, and
libcamera always turns both on for this camera (it is mounted rotated by 180
degrees) and picks the binned mode for every request of 1280x720 or smaller.

Base:    linux-surface/kernel, branch v7.3-surface, drivers/media/i2c/ov5693.c
         as of commit 00a71904ce4a ("media: i2c: Expand gain values for
         ov5693"); the file kernel-surface 7.3.4-2 was built from
         (SHA-256 bbb12e8e715669037f4a4a164d488df3ec11b5fa78e6b90b04e321d8208fdbc1)
Changes: the ov5693.c changes of rylos/kernel, branch sp5-ipu3-cameras, at
         8e3833974a7f (pull request linux-surface/kernel#181), which carry
         D. Manresa's binned-mode patch from linux-surface/linux-surface#2252:
           - mode registers programmed on every stream start
           - binned readout geometry, PLL and analogue values from the Windows
             driver's mode tables, 30 fps binned values by default
           - only the sensor-side vertical flip bit in the binned mode
           - default frame rate capped at 30 fps
           - Bayer phase kept when exactly one flip is on at full resolution
Local:   - the unconditional MIPI_CTRL00 (0x4800) = 0x2d write is replaced by
           the mipi_ctrl00 module parameter, off by default: the IPU4P of the
           Surface Pro 7 streams with the register's power-on value
         - mirror module parameter: inverts the horizontal flip, so the
           picture is flipped left to right in every application (the idea is
           surface-kit's ov5693 mirror parameter; here it also feeds the
           Bayer phase compensation above, so the colours stay right)

